s -> t sign ledger
------------------
t=-is, s=it, d^2/ds^2=-d^2/dt^2, s^3=-it^3, s=it.
A=10/3^(5/4),
B_R=[2-2delta-4sqrt(3)(n+1/2)]/3^(3/4),
B_I=[2-2delta+4sqrt(3)(n+1/2)]/3^(3/4).
The rotated differential perturbation is P_I=i(A t^3-B_I t).
Harmonic-oscillator form contains -P_I, and therefore
(H0-2n-1)u1_I=-P_I phi_n and c_j,I=-<n+j|P_I|n>_B/(2j).
The cubic and linear pieces have opposite relative signs.

Corrected u1 coefficients
-------------------------
Writing u1_sigma=sum_j c_j,sigma phi_(n+j), j=-3,-1,1,3, with negative
indices omitted:

c_-3,R= 5 sqrt(2) 3^(3/4) sqrt[n(n-1)(n-2)]/108
c_-1,R=-sqrt(2) 3^(1/4) sqrt(n)(2delta-sqrt(3)n-2+2sqrt(3))/12
c_1,R= sqrt(2) 3^(1/4) sqrt(n+1)(2delta-sqrt(3)n-3sqrt(3)-2)/12
c_3,R=-5 sqrt(2) 3^(3/4) sqrt[(n+1)(n+2)(n+3)]/108

c_-3,I= i 5 sqrt(2) 3^(3/4) sqrt[n(n-1)(n-2)]/108
c_-1,I= i sqrt(2) 3^(1/4) sqrt(n)(2delta+sqrt(3)n-2sqrt(3)-2)/12
c_1,I=-i sqrt(2) 3^(1/4) sqrt(n+1)(2delta+sqrt(3)n-2+3sqrt(3))/12
c_3,I=-i 5 sqrt(2) 3^(3/4) sqrt[(n+1)(n+2)(n+3)]/108

Exact first-order substitution
------------------------------
Hermite recurrence substitution gives identically zero residual for the
real and imaginary inhomogeneous equations.  Exact checks were performed
for n=0,1,2,3,4, including boundary-state omission.  General symbolic
matrix-element identities were checked for all four shifts.  Both diagonal
odd matrix elements vanish.

Residual checks
---------------
- Coefficient truncation: R-R0=q R1+O(q^2), exactly; numerical ratios tend
  to 2 when q is halved.  This is residual/u0 only away from zeros of u0.
- Corrected wavefunction: direct substitution of u0+q u1 in the exact local
  coefficient gives absolute residual O(q^2), without division by u0.
  For n=1, delta=0.7, successive halving ratios were
  R: 4.05998, 4.02967; I: 3.99942, 3.99985.
  Tests also cover both branches for n=0,1,2 and three detunings.

Second-order solvability
------------------------
Real branch: <W_R>_B+<V_R u1_R>_B=0.
Imaginary branch: (H0-E_n)u2_I=-P_I u1_I+T_I phi_n and hence
<T_I>_B-<P_I u1_I>_B=0, where T_I=W_s(it).
All direct even terms, e2, and all n+-1,n+-3 intermediate states were kept.
Both exact expressions reduce to

sqrt(3)[24delta^2-12delta+72e2+6n^2+6n+1]/108=0,

so independently
e2_R=e2_I=delta(1-2delta)/6-(6n^2+6n+1)/72.
The exact difference between e2_I and the Stage 08 operator target is zero.
That comparison was made only after the local calculation.

